OL,3,GNEWSAD-Day veteran celebrates 103rd
OL,4,Abirthday
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former Royal Marine commando who
OL,7,Fhelped clear mines from a Normandy
OL,8,Fbeach during D-Day is celebrating his
OL,9,F103rd birthday.
OL,11,FJames Laughlin was one of 17,000 Royal
OL,12,FMarines involved in D-Day. Armed only
OL,13,Fwith a knife between his teeth, he swam
OL,14,Fto Gold Beach to clear mines that posed
OL,15,Fa danger to landing craft.
OL,17,FNatacha Atkinson, manager of Belvedere
OL,18,Fcare home in Accrington, Lancashire,
OL,19,Fwhere the veteran lives, described him
OL,20,Fas "cheeky".
OL,23,APub: 18-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
